    "vin_structure": "17 chars: pos1-3=WMI, pos4-8=VDS, pos9=check_digit, pos10=model_year, pos11=plant, pos12-17=serial",
    "vds_note": "Ford follows NHTSA format strictly as a US OEM. VDS is one of the most rigorously documented due to NHTSA filing requirements. All positions 4-8 carry meaningful attribute data for all markets. pos9 = NHTSA check digit for all US/Canada VINs.",
    "gcc_note": "Ford vehicles in UAE/GCC are predominantly US-built (1FT F-150/Raptor, 1FA Mustang). F-150 Raptor is the dominant Ford in GCC market. European-market Fords (WF0/WF9) use different position encoding.",
    "european_note": "WF0 (Ford-Werke Germany) European VINs follow ISO 3779 not NHTSA. European Fords (Puma, Focus, Fiesta, Kuga) use different pos4-8 encoding — separate tables needed. This file covers North American format primarily."
  },

